id: monstrous-vitality
name: Monstrous Vitality
order: 1
category: body
importance: primary
# (1) A Monstrous Trait and a Bestial Trait, each chosen as it is added - gone with it.
grantsOther: monstrous, bestial
description: >
  Powerful and sturdy, Creatures are hard to put down.
text: >
  Monstrous Vitality (Body): Powerful and sturdy, Creatures are hard to put down.
  (1)-[Passive]: At Character Creation, select and gain access to a Monstrous Trait and a Bestial Trait.
  (2)-[Passive]: Your Life Points can exceed your Maximum Life Points by an amount equal to 1/2 of your Maximum Life Points.
  (3)-[Triggered/Injured]: Use a Healing Surge as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (4)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Encounter]: Use a Healing Surge as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.

---

[passive]
# (2) Life Points regained up to half the Maximum past it, rounded down (actor-character.mjs life.ceiling).
allow monstrousVitality.overflow;

# (3) Knocked through the Injured Health Threshold: a Healing Surge out of sequence - chosen on the Threshold's card, never Automatic.
[triggered/threshold, outOfSequence, effect 3]
requires knockedThrough("injured");
surge(healing);

# (4) The Combat Encounter begins: a Healing Surge out of sequence - chosen on its card, never Automatic.
[triggered/start-of-encounter, outOfSequence, effect 4]
surge(healing);
